Z||000000||Gokart||10-07-1999||07:38 PM||||I have been given an opportunity to buy a 85 Coupe with a very low miles rebuilt V6 engine and a stainless steel exhaust. I can only buy it for parts cause the mechanic cannot get the title, previous owner is deceased and family won't pay for work that had been done, so no title. Originally it was a 4 cyl. My question is what do you think I should offer him for it and could I use anything else on it for parts besides the engine and exhaust for my fastback?||||reg||5
Z||000001||RZURCTN||10-07-1999||07:57 PM||||I would say that if the mechanic could not recover the cost of repairs from the family, he could put a lein against the vehicle and still obtain a title to it.  If the family refuses to pay, take it to court.  But you may end up with nothing.  I don't know the particular laws where you are from.  I say consult the DMV or your neighborhood attorney.  Or have the guy send it to a salvage yard where you can re-obtain it with a salvage title?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||10-07-1999||08:35 PM||||The mechanic should be able to file for an abandoned vehicle title. We have seen it done several times for this same situation because the owners have abandoned the vehicle in the care of the mechanic. It is not hard to do in Alabama, but your state may be different. Check your DMV for details.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Gokart||10-07-1999||09:21 PM||||I know he doesn't want to go through any of that with the car. He's strickly a BMW/Volvo mechanic and the work done on the Fiero was done on the side by another ex-employee. It's been sitting behind his shop for at least 2 years now. I'm not concerned with putting the car on the road. I'll take the engine and exhaust and was wondering if anything else would be of use for my fastback? Then I'd peice it out for anyone that could use the parts that I can't. So...what else would be of use and how much would you pay!? ||||reg||2
Z||000004||batboy||10-07-1999||10:54 PM||||Almost all the parts are interchangeable with a few exceptions.||||reg||1
